{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK7qoGWBQNFTZQnHueBY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`STATIC_URL` and `MEDIA_URL` now get the current `SCRIPT_NAME` prefix when they're relative. I made the change in `LazySettings.__getattr__` in `django/conf/__init__.py`. Values that start with `/`, `http://` or `https://` are left alone, so existing setups behave as before.\n\nI ran `settings_tests`, `staticfiles_tests` and `file_storage`. Two `setUpClass` errors (`StaticLiveServerView`, `FileLikeObjectTestCase`) also occur without my change.\n\nMy change adds four `file_storage` failures, all in `test_setting_changed`. That test overrides `MEDIA_URL` with the relative value `'overridden_media_url/'` and compares the storage's `base_url` against the raw setting. Under the new behaviour `base_url` is now `'/overridden_media_url/'`, so the test's expected value needs the leading slash. I didn't touch test files, per the rules.\n\nI didn't add a regression test or exercise a non-default `SCRIPT_NAME`.\n\nThe prefixed value is cached the first time a setting is read. A later change to `SCRIPT_NAME` in the same process won't show up in an already-read `STATIC_URL` or `MEDIA_URL`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495,"cache_read_input_tokens":24482,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":495},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a36218d6-2921-4e49-a157-08c019e9071f","uuid":"fd345cb3-a162-4626-aacc-ddf0ae4e61e3","timestamp":"2026-11-23T03:04:48.655Z","request_id":"req_011ChK7qo94ucdrHoH9g9gvT"}
